content.thinking:
Wait, there's a subtle issue with `plan_reconstruct` and the BFS numbering: the children of node `self` are numbered self+1 .. self+kids, but the recursive calls put descendants in between! Let me re-read:

```cpp
size_t self = out.size();
out.push_back(n);            // index self
for z: plan_reconstruct(child z)   // appends child z's subtree at indices self+1, ...
for z: out[self].children.push_back(self+1+z);
```
This is wrong: after the first recursive call, the child's whole subtree is appended, so child 1's own subtree occupies indices self+1 .. self+size(subtree0). Setting children = self+1+z is only correct for BFS order (i.e., children are numbered consecutively right after the parent), which is NOT the pre-order numbering produced by the recursion.

So the reconstruction numbering is pre-order (DFS), while children ids are wrongly set. I need to:
1. Build the tree with pre-order numbering and correct child ids, then renumber to BFS.

Let me restructure: build a temporary tree in DFS order recording the actual child indices, then renumber by BFS.

Simplest: recursive function returning the node index in a pre-order list, with children recorded properly; then renumber.

Renumbering: BFS traversal of the pre-order tree → new ids; map old→new; then output nodes in new order with children mapped.

Let me rewrite plan_reconstruct:

```cpp
static int plan_build(const VersionPlan& vp, int i, int j, int c, std::vector<Layout>& pre) {
    const PlanDec& d = vp.pick(i,j,c);
    Layout n; n.lo=i; n.span=j-i; n.mode=d.mode; n.cached=d.cached;
    size_t self = pre.size();
    pre.push_back(n);
    int kids = (int)d.cs.size();
    for (int z=0;z<kids;++z) {
        int id = plan_build(vp, d.cs[z], d.ce[z], d.buds[z], pre);
        pre[self].children.push_back(id);
    }
    return (int)self;
}
static void plan_reconstruct(...) {
   std::vector<Layout> pre; plan_build(vp,0,R,cap,pre);
   // BFS renumber
   std::vector<int> q; q.push_back(0);
   for (size_t k=0;k<q.size();++k) for (int ch: pre[q[k]].children) q.push_back(ch);
   std::vector<int> map(pre.size());
   for (size_t k=0;k<q.size();++k) map[q[k]] = (int)k;
   out.assign(pre.size(), Layout());
   for (size_t k=0;k<pre.size();++k) {
      const Layout& n = pre[q[k]];
      Layout m; m.lo=n.lo;m.span=n.span;m.mode=n.mode;m.cached=n.cached;
      for (int ch : n.children) m.children.push_back(map[ch]);
      out[k]=m;
   }
}
```
Also verify q.size()==pre.size() (all reachable).

Note that plan_build recursion depth ≤ 6 ✓.

